"""Generate a compact, printable A4 model card from recorded evaluation artifacts."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
m=json.loads((ROOT/'dist/data/metrics.json').read_text())
rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{h["horizonHours"]}h</td><td>{h["testRows"]:,}</td><td>{h["targets"]["od07"]["model"]["accuracy"]:.2%}</td><td>{h["targets"]["od07"]["weatherRules"]["accuracy"]:.2%}</td><td>{h["targets"]["od07"]["model"]["brier"]:.4f}</td><td>{h["targets"]["od07"]["weatherRules"]["brier"]:.4f}</td></tr>' for h in m['horizons'])
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>FRA WindLab · One-page model card</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#eef1f3;color:#203142;font:11.5px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif}main{width:790px;max-width:100%;margin:25px auto;padding:35px 38px;background:white;border-top:7px solid #a6d978}h1{font-size:29px;letter-spacing:-1px;margin:5px 0}h2{font-size:13px;margin:18px 0 5px}p{margin:5px 0 10px}.eyebrow{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:2px;color:#6d8460}.sub{color:#687d8b}.alert{background:#fff3e4;border-left:3px solid #cf9d62;padding:11px 13px;margin:15px 0}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:11px}td,th{padding:7px 5px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #e3e9ed}th{font-weight:600;color:#6b7c87;background:#f5f7f8}.columns{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:25px}a{color:#52783d;text-underline-offset:2px}.sources{border-top:1px solid #dbe3e8;margin-top:15px;padding-top:12px;font-size:10px}.toolbar{width:790px;max-width:100%;margin:20px auto -10px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:12px}.toolbar button{border:0;padding:8px 13px;background:#172737;color:white;border-radius:5px;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:600px){main{padding:22px}.columns{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:0}.toolbar{padding:0 15px}table{font-size:9px}td,th{padding:6px 3px}}@page{size:A4;margin:12mm}@media print{body{background:white;font-size:8.5pt;line-height:1.36}.toolbar{display:none}main{width:auto;margin:0;padding:8mm 0 0;border-top-width:4px}h1{font-size:22pt}h2{margin-top:11px;font-size:10pt}table{font-size:8pt}td,th{padding:5px}.columns{gap:6mm}.sources{font-size:7.5pt}.alert{margin:10px 0;padding:9px}a{color:inherit}p{margin-bottom:7px}}</style></head><body>
<div class="toolbar"><a href="./">← Dashboard</a><button onclick="window.print()">Print / save PDF</button></div><main><div class="eyebrow">AI WEEK 2026 · FRAALLIANCE CHALLENGE · V1.1 · 30 OCT 2026</div><h1>FRA WindLab · Model card</h1><p class="sub">48-hour hourly probabilities for RWY 18 wind usability and operating direction 07 / 25.</p>
<div class="alert"><strong>Research model · weather-derived targets.</strong> No historical airport operation labels were obtained. Scores assess wind-rule proxies, not actual operations. At 50%, the model misses all 5 test closure-proxy hours. The new alert modes use fixed sensitivity thresholds plus wind-limit overrides; operational calibration remains unverified.</div>
<h2>Two alert priorities · scheduled hours only</h2><p><strong>Catch more closures (1%):</strong> at 1h, detects 3/3 proxy closure hours with 116 false alarms (2.5% precision). <strong>Reduce false alarms (10%):</strong> detects 0/3 with 4 false alarms. At 6h / 24h / 48h, catch mode detects 2/3 / 1/3 / 0/3; reduce mode detects none. Both override on forecast wind-limit exceedance. This reuses the known holdout; thresholds were not optimized. Rare events and weak validation preclude a reliability claim.</p><h2>Held-out direction-proxy results</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Lead</th><th>Test hours</th><th>ML accuracy</th><th>Rules accuracy</th><th>ML Brier ↓</th><th>Rules Brier ↓</th></tr></thead><tbody>ROWS</tbody></table><p class="sub">ML improves classification at 1h/6h; rules classify better at 24h/48h. Brier measures probability error. Baseline uses the same archived weather inputs. No test-driven retuning.</p>
<div class="columns"><div><h2>Data & targets</h2><p>49,600 EDDF METAR reports, Jan 2024–Oct 2026, plus archived DWD ICON forecasts. Variable/missing wind direction is excluded. Missing METAR gusts use sustained wind; only 1.36% explicitly report gusts. Airport closure logs are unavailable.</p>
<h2>Learning & key drivers</h2><p>Separate L2 logistic regressions for closure and OD07 at 1, 6, 24 and 48h. Features: forecast wind vectors, gusts and runway components; prior observed wind and 3h trends; origin direction; time and season. Training-only standardization; regularization selected by validation Brier score. Intermediate hours use the nearest horizon model.</p>
<h2>Flight hours &amp; challenge rules</h2><p>Scheduled takeoffs/landings: <strong>05:00–23:00 Europe/Berlin</strong>, including DST. Night restrictions are independent of weather. Before midnight, eligible delayed landings may arrive; delayed departures need permission. Exceptional flights remain possible.</p><p>Headings 180°, 070°, 250° true. RWY18 tailwind ≥15 kt or gust crosswind &gt;40 kt means wind restriction. OD switches at ≥10 kt tailwind, or smaller adverse wind persisting &gt;30 min. Fraport public guidance uses a different 5 kt landing threshold; this model follows the supplied challenge.</p></div>
<div><h2>Time splits & leakage controls</h2><p>Train: 2024–2025. Validation: 4 Jan–31 Mar 2026. Test: 4 Apr–29 Oct 2026. Splits have 72h gaps. Origins use only prior METARs, at most 40min old. Target observations never enter origin features. Archived forecast leads: 24h for 1h/6h models, 48h for 24h, 72h for 48h, all predating origins.</p>
<h2>Limits that affect interpretation</h2><p>Live ICON inputs are fresher than backtest inputs. Probabilities are logistic scores without independent operational calibration. Only 28–34 training and 5 all-hour / 3 scheduled-hour test closure proxies support each model. Hourly output cannot resolve minute-level changes. No switch-event timing validation. Controller decisions, aircraft restrictions, works, and upper-air wind are not modeled.</p>
<h2>Reproduction & next evidence</h2><p>Run the downloader, training script and snapshot builder; exported coefficients run in Python/JavaScript. Historical replay accepts an issue time after model selection. Add verified operational histories and untouched future jury days before claiming airport operating accuracy.</p></div></div>
<div class="sources"><strong>Sources:</strong> <a href="https://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu/request/download.phtml">IEM METAR</a> · <a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/docs/previous-runs-api">Open-Meteo Previous Runs</a> · <a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/docs/dwd-api">DWD ICON via Open-Meteo</a> · <a href="https://aviationweather.gov/data/api/">NOAA AWC</a> · <a href="https://www.umwelthaus.org/fluglaerm/anwendungen-service/aktuelle-betriebsrichtung-und-prognose/">Umwelthaus / DFS</a>. Rules: user-supplied FraAlliance case PDF; audio confirms the task.<br><a href="data/metrics.json">Model metrics</a> · <a href="data/alert-policies.json">Alert comparisons</a> · <a href="https://www.fraport.com/en/sustainability/dialog-with-neighbors/noise-and-air/flight-operations/runway-system-and-operating-hours.html">Fraport hours</a> · <a href="https://wirtschaft.hessen.de/Verkehr/Luftverkehr/Verspaetete-Starts-und-Landungen">Hessen exceptions</a> · <a href="data/model.json">Trained model</a> · Data/model timestamps retained in downloadable artifacts.</div></main></body></html>'''
(ROOT/'dist/model-card.html').write_text(html.replace('ROWS',rows),encoding='utf8')
